 "method": "Citywide value = sum of the BA (business applications) columns for counties 36005, 36047, 36061, 36081 and 36085 in the Census county-level annual BFS file. Peer value = 2025 applications in the principal county / Vintage 2025 July 1 population x 1,000.",
 "caveats": [
  "An application for an EIN is not a business opening: many applications never become businesses with employees, and the count includes sole proprietors, holding companies and other entities.",
  "Applications are placed in a county from the address on the application, which may not be where the business actually operates.",
  "Applications jumped in 2020 and 2021 and have stayed well above pre-2020 levels; the county file does not show how many of them became operating businesses."
 ]
